---Git repo configuration for a single cluster.
---@class gcp.unstable.gkehub_v1alpha.ConfigManagementGitConfig
---@field policyDir? string Optional. The path within the Git repository that represents the top level of the repo to sync. Default: the root directory of the repository.
---@field httpsProxy? string Optional. URL for the HTTPS proxy to be used when communicating with the Git repo. Defines an HTTPS_PROXY environment variable and only accepts `https` or unadorned URLs. For example, `https://proxy.internal.business.co:443` or `proxy.internal.business.co:443`. If using an unadorned URL, make sure the communication between your proxy server and Git host is secure. Rejects `http://` URLs. Only specify when secret_type is `cookiefile`, `token`, or `none`.
---@field syncRepo? string Required. The URL of the Git repository to use as the source of truth.
---@field syncRev? string Optional. Git revision (tag or hash) or branch to sync from. Default `HEAD`. If not `HEAD`, takes precedence over `sync_branch` field. When using a hash, must be a full hash, and not an abbreviated form.
---@field gcpServiceAccountEmail? string Optional. The Google Cloud Service Account Email used for auth when secret_type is `gcpserviceaccount`. Annotates the `RootSync` or `RepoSync` controller's Kubernetes Service Account.
---@field secretType? string Required. Type of secret configured for access to the Git repo. Must be one of `ssh`, `cookiefile`, `gcenode`, `token`, `gcpserviceaccount`, `githubapp` or `none`. The validation of this is case-sensitive.
---@field syncWaitSecs? string Optional. Period in seconds between consecutive syncs. Default: 15.
---@field syncBranch? string Optional. The branch of the repository to sync from. Default: master.

