---@class gcp.unstable.gkehub_v1alpha.UpgradeProjectsLocationsRolloutSequencesRequest
---@field patchOnly? boolean Optional. If set to true, the rollout will only upgrade clusters that match the minor version of the `version` field, but are on an earlier patch version.
---@field prioritized? boolean Optional. If set to true, conflicting rollouts will be paused, to allow this rollout to progress through the sequence. Conflicting rollouts running on the first stage will be canceled, to allow this rollout to be created.
---@field soakDurationOverrideAllStages? string Optional. Overrides the soak duration for all stages of the rollout.
---@field upgradeType? gcp.unstable.gkehub_v1alpha.UpgradeRolloutSequenceRequestUpgradeTypeEnum|string Required. The type of upgrade.
---@field ignoreMaintenancePolicies? boolean Optional. If set to true, the rollout will ignore any maintenance policies (Maintenance Windows and Maintenance Exclusions) set on the clusters.
---@field version? string Required. GKE version to upgrade to. A valid GKE version available on the release channel used by the sequence. Patch versions from less conservative channels are allowed if their minor version is already available in the sequence's channel. This is similar to single-cluster upgrade rules, see https://cloud.google.com/kubernetes-engine/docs/how-to/upgrading-a-cluster#supported-versions Example: With the following versions available on the RAPID and REGULAR channels: * REGULAR: 1.35.3-gke.123000 * RAPID: 1.36.4-gke.321000, 1.35.6-gke.045000 Valid versions are 1.35.3-gke.123, 1.35.6-gke.045000 Aliases like `latest` are supported. For more information on valid upgrade versions and specifying cluster versions, see: https://cloud.google.com/kubernetes-engine/versioning#specifying_cluster_version
---@field force? boolean Optional. If set to true, any rollout already running on the first stage of the sequence will be cancelled to allow for the creation of the new rollout.
---@field soakDurationOverridePerStage? gcp.unstable.gkehub_v1alpha.PerStageSoakDurationOverrides Optional. Overrides the soak durations for specific stages of the rollout.
---@field ignoreClusterDisruptionBudgets? boolean Optional. If set to true, the rollout will ignore the disruption budgets of the clusters.
---@field name string Required. The name of the rollout sequence. Format: projects/{project}/locations/{location}/rolloutSequences/{rollout_sequence}

---@alias gcp.unstable.gkehub_v1alpha.UpgradeRolloutSequenceRequestUpgradeTypeEnum "UPGRADE_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"CONTROL_PLANE"|"NODE"

